cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use APAURA, please cite this software."
title: "APAURA: Alternative Polyadenylation Architecture, Usage, and Regulatory Analysis"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Boateng-Sarfo"
    given-names: "George"
  - family-names: "Niewold"
    given-names: "Erica"
  - family-names: "Sigor"
    given-names: "Sarah"
  - family-names: "Wang"
    given-names: "Lili"

version: "0.10.1"
date-released: "2026-10-06"
license: GPL-3.0-only

repository-code: "https://github.com/gsarfo-boateng/APAURA"
url: "https://github.com/gsarfo-boateng/APAURA"

abstract: >-
  APAURA is a Java toolkit for alternative polyadenylation architecture,
  usage, differential mechanism analysis, protocol-aware 3'-end sequencing,
  direct-RNA and long-read analysis, conventional short-read RNA-seq,
  single-cell APA analysis, regulatory motif enrichment, and locus
  visualization.

keywords:
  - alternative polyadenylation
  - polyadenylation
  - RNA-seq
  - 3' end sequencing
  - direct RNA sequencing
  - 3' UTR
  - alternative last exon
  - intronic polyadenylation
  - RNA-binding proteins
  - bioinformatics
